      "notes": "Governance, from the S-1 cover. Anthropic is a Delaware public benefit corporation. Its stated purpose: the responsible development and maintenance of advanced AI for the long-term benefit of humanity. The Long-Term Benefit Trust, an independent body of financially disinterested trustees, generally elects and removes the Class T directors, who form a board majority. One Class F share, held by the Founder LLC, carries 50.1% of total voting power on general matters and has no economic rights. Class A shares (the ones sold in the IPO) carry one vote each. Anthropic will be a Nasdaq 'controlled company'.\n\nSource:\n- SEC EDGAR, Form S-1 cover page: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2130357/000162828026067168/anthropicpbc-sx1.htm"
    },
